WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:04.750
- Many of us have been asked to find X.

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:07.380
But for something to be found,

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:10.280
it must first have been lost.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.480
(gentle music)

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:16.113
On the number line, life was well defined.

00:00:17.899 --> 00:00:20.590
(rocket engine roaring)

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:23.640
With prized fields and blue skies,

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.713
things were pretty organized.

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:30.780
Until one non-ordinary day

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:33.463
when all patterns went astray.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:37.360
This is the story of X

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:40.440
who was born, to shock and surprise,

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.773
with an equation too tough to analyze.

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:49.350
X's parents were 40 and 42.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:52.500
But after 41 came between them,

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:55.185
40 had moved on with someone new.

00:00:55.185 --> 00:00:56.393
(door shuts)

00:00:56.393 --> 00:00:58.490
(bus engine whirring)
(numbers chattering)

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:02.550
Growing up, X's life
felt far from optimal,

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:06.383
since without a value,
how can one be valuable?

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:09.983
One day,

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:15.880
a school trip to the function
fair turned to despair

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:17.213
when X was told,

00:01:18.407 --> 00:01:21.760
"You must have this value to ride,"

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:25.323
and was sent instead to the minimal slide.

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:31.680
That night at the times table,

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:34.830
relational emotions were unstable.

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:38.550
X blamed 42 for their missing value.

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:42.420
42 snapped back, "It isn't all about you.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:46.633
If only you were numeric, that
would simplify my life too.

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:51.507
I'm tired of this pointless
search for your value."

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.403
X slammed their door and began to cry.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:00.267
42 cooled off, knocked,

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:01.530
(door thuds)

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.367
but no reply.

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:07.570
"X, I'm sorry for what I said to you.

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:10.373
I was out of order. It wasn't true.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:14.087
Please know that I value you."

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:20.410
But already outside,
eyes blurred by misery,

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:23.273
X had not heard 42's apology.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:28.163
Untying their old boat, cold and scared,

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:32.773
X hadn't realized that
their pain was shared.

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:38.520
Every night, 42 worked on finding X,

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:41.770
even when the math became complex.

00:02:41.770 --> 00:02:45.050
42 worked with increased ferocity.

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:48.290
Their working was an absolute monstrosity,

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:51.273
they'd even found a fictional velocity.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:55.713
X sailed out far into the ocean,

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:00.883
battling the elements and their emotions,

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:03.960
when a sinusoidal storm

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:06.780
rose with an unbalanced force,

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:10.583
sending the boat and X curving off-course.

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:16.323
Spotting an island, X gave a shout,

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:20.337
before the boom swung
around and knocked X out.

00:03:26.778 --> 00:03:29.567
(water gently splashing)

00:03:29.567 --> 00:03:32.560
(seagulls chirping)

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:36.603
Washed up on the beach, X barely survived,

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:40.453
but was discovered by a group of Is.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:44.850
(volcano erupts)

00:03:45.847 --> 00:03:49.730
Part of an ancient numerical civilization

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:53.143
who had an archaic
system of classification.

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:01.290
X woke to an Emperor's voice

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:05.157
who peered down giving X no choice.

00:04:05.157 --> 00:04:07.920
"This one will be useful later.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:11.570
I declare them a 10, a gladiator."

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:16.570
Then, M leaned down with a
menacing demeanor and said,

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:20.517
"You can prove your value in the arena."

00:04:22.591 --> 00:04:27.591
(intense music)
(crowd cheering)

00:04:30.859 --> 00:04:33.692
(swords clanking)

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:39.170
X thought maybe they'd
found a way to belong

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:43.063
with this group of 10s so big and strong.

00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:48.210
But something felt so terribly wrong.

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:51.390
Everyone expected X to fight.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:54.379
Swords drawn, the crowd
roared with delight.

00:04:54.379 --> 00:04:57.530
(crowd cheering)

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:00.340
When two angles of radiant light

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:04.400
flew through X's line of sight,

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:07.843
their movement inspired X to try,

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:12.113
folding up into an I.

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:17.450
This way, X escaped from the jail house,

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:22.253
grateful for all the practice
of trying to be someone else.

00:05:23.105 --> 00:05:26.158
(ominous music)
(Is grunting)

00:05:26.158 --> 00:05:28.491
(X panting)

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:38.190
Then down the shaft of an old mine,

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:40.863
X fell to the axis line.

00:05:42.470 --> 00:05:45.660
Lost in a dark and dingy nook,

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:48.710
X discovered an ancient book.

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:51.470
It spanned all of mathematics

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:54.923
from algebra to geometry to quadratics.

00:05:56.530 --> 00:06:00.830
X was shocked to see on almost every page

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:03.783
that their name was center stage.

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:10.090
Blinking, bewildered, it made no sense.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:12.720
X flipped to the back with suspense

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:16.500
where the answers should be
listed, but nothing there.

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.909
No answers existed.

00:06:18.909 --> 00:06:20.870
(walls rumbling)

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:25.020
The walls around X then
congruently shifted

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:27.670
glowing beads on an abacus drifted

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:32.983
to reveal a bright and
welcoming direction.

00:06:35.727 --> 00:06:39.033
"Much better than here,"
X thought on reflection.

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:43.293
(bright music)

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:51.170
X was on cloud nine.

00:06:51.170 --> 00:06:53.820
This place was divine.

00:06:53.820 --> 00:06:55.890
It was hard to define,

00:06:55.890 --> 00:07:00.050
but unlike anything
else on the number line.

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:04.440
There were strange symbols
X had never seen before.

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:07.723
It wasn't clear what they even stood for.

00:07:09.210 --> 00:07:13.350
One said, "Hello, X. Come through.

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:16.093
I'm Y. It's nice to meet you.

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:23.100
Welcome to the Origin, the
place where number lines begin."

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:27.550
Y was the first unknown X had talked to,

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:31.580
so X asked, "Do you know your value?"

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:35.950
Y nodded, replying, "And so shall you.

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:38.437
Let me change your point of view."

00:07:40.070 --> 00:07:45.070
Y led X on a tour of math
that was wonderfully obscure.

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:47.417
Then Y said,

00:07:47.417 --> 00:07:51.800
"Knowing your value can
be an irrational endeavor.

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:55.583
Pi knows theirs but will
be chasing it forever.

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:00.070
You must come to grips with the fact

00:08:00.070 --> 00:08:02.483
math is not about your value.

00:08:03.410 --> 00:08:06.849
Math is about relationships.

00:08:06.849 --> 00:08:09.599
(majestic music)

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:17.783
You and I can form a line,

00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:19.943
a circle,

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:23.833
or an ellipse.

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:29.043
We're like magicians with
transformative tricks.

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:36.097
And with that, the whole
grid is at our fingertips."

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:41.900
Seeing that it's okay to be unknown,

00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:46.197
X said, "Let's solve this
problem of getting me home."

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:58.633
On X's return, 42 was overjoyed,

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:04.470
saying, "Life without you
felt like 0: a complete void."

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:09.230
X felt a healing deep in their heart

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:12.680
at this reunion of broken parts.

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:17.620
42 invited X into their exclusive space,

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:20.080
where there was a briefcase

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:24.463
full of equations and
formulae half erased.

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:30.150
42 proved to X that they'd
always been working,

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:34.000
never given up hope,
never stopped searching.

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:38.620
X and 42 embraced, X happily crying

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:42.643
to see how hard 42 had been trying.

00:09:43.910 --> 00:09:47.650
Before the papers could
cause any more pain,

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:52.580
X threw them out into a new domain.

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:55.610
An answer was no longer needed,

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:59.677
and as the tears receded, X said,

00:09:59.677 --> 00:10:02.973
"To blame you, 42, was wrong.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:05.433
I found my value.

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:08.967
It was here all along."

00:10:10.529 --> 00:10:12.946
(warm music)

00:10:46.026 --> 00:10:48.693
(water flowing)

00:11:05.111 --> 00:11:07.944
(papers rustling)

